  "claimed_state": "Fixed-step old-particle position residual on three exact clock nodes and contact-qualified material rows. Includes the actual free-velocity action and its residual derivatives, plus prescribed endpoint velocity, position candidate, and residual derivatives. The material history correspondence comes from caller-supplied snapshots.",
  "verification": {
    "ctest": [
      "coupling.case_uniform_flow",
      "aero.global_geometry",
      "aero.p1_shared_action",
      "coupling.case_motion_time_series"
    ],
    "catch": "Free wake motion uses all sources at attached and inherited material points, seed 23; 518 assertions.",
    "oracle": "Fraction evaluation of same-interval BDF2 over exact eighth-second steps; 75-decimal inherited independent GL88 induction/JVP at the second receiver; analytic polynomial prescribed velocity with independent candidate, direction, and transpose work.",
    "negative": "Swapped times, stale release epoch, use of attached trailing-edge point, wrong original Case, prescribed mode supplied to a free evaluator, resource ceiling, and stop request.",
    "msvc_release": "Windows x64 MSVC 19.51 Release, four affected CTests passed.",
    "gcc": "Ubuntu Noble x64 GCC 14.2 Release, build with warnings as errors; four affected CTests passed.",
    "mutation": "In the separate Linux build, supplying the positive velocity seed instead of the negative seed failed the physical transpose pairing (1 of 518 assertions, exit 42). Restoring byte-identical product source and rebuilding passed all 518 assertions.",
    "stack": "The existing load transpose's zero-RHS-budget rejection nested two fixed-width rounding scratch blocks. Reusing its caller's block removed the duplicate while preserving the unchanged projection checks and a 1 MiB MSVC test stack.",
    "static": "Pinned clang-format 21.1.2, clang-tidy 21.1.1 on affected units in both environments, reference regeneration, Ruff and Japanese prose lint, trace-check, and source/artifact hash comparison.",
    "msvc_debug": "Windows x64 MSVC 19.51 Debug, four affected CTests passed. coupling.case_uniform_flow completed in 65.53 s (120 s limit), and the focused case passed 518 assertions with seed 23.",
    "review_base": "e518c6c4e496998510ad177bf7d629e56ecda20b",
    "review_case": "With h=1/8 s, positions (2, 15/8, 13/8) and directions (1/8, 1/4, 1/2) give distinct exact BDF2 (1/2,-1/2) and backward Euler (1,-1) time derivatives. Both production transport paths use rational comparisons of residuals, JVPs and three stencil covectors.",
    "review_msvc_release": "Windows x64 MSVC 19.51 Release; 548 focused assertions passed with seed 23.",
    "review_backward_euler_mutation": "Only transport_rate was replaced with (current-previous)/h. The focused MSVC Release run rejected 7 of 548 assertions, exit 42. The byte-identical restored product source rebuilt and passed all 548 assertions."
